    <ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>A legislative summary is currently being prepared for this bill by the Parliamentary Information and Research Service of the Library of Parliament. Meanwhile, the following executive summary is available. 

On 12 June 2009, The Minister of State (Democratic Reform) introduced Bill C-40, An Act to amend the Canada Elections Act (Expanded Voting Opportunities Act), in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.

Bill C-16 makes various amendments to the Canada Elections Act.  It increases the number of advance polling days from three to four and increases the number of polling stations open on the last day of advance polling.</ShortLegislativeSummaryEn>
    <ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>Le Service d'information et de recherche parlementaires de la Bibliothèque du Parlement rédige actuellement le résumé législatif de ce projet de loi. Entre-temps, il met à votre disposition le sommaire suivant. 

Le 12 juin 2009, Le ministre d'État (Réforme démocratique) a déposé le projet de loi C-40, Loi modifiant la Loi électorale du Canada (Loi sur les possibilités de vote accrues), à la Chambre des communes en première lecture.

Le projet de loi apporte diverses modifications à la Loi électorale du Canada.  Il fait passer de trois à quatre le nombre de jours de vote par anticipation et augmente le nombre de bureaux de vote par anticipation ouverts le dernier jour du vote par anticipation.</ShortLegislativeSummaryFr>
    <ShortLegislativeSummary>A legislative summary is currently being prepared for this bill by the Parliamentary Information and Research Service of the Library of Parliament. Meanwhile, the following executive summary is available. 

On 12 June 2009, The Minister of State (Democratic Reform) introduced Bill C-40, An Act to amend the Canada Elections Act (Expanded Voting Opportunities Act), in the House of Commons and it was given first reading.

Bill C-16 makes various amendments to the Canada Elections Act.  It increases the number of advance polling days from three to four and increases the number of polling stations open on the last day of advance polling.</ShortLegislativeSummary>
